nd is 6-high, no made hand, missed flush draw. Opponent is passive but called turn bet, suggesting at least a weak pair or Ace-high. Pot is small (200). Bluff has low chance of success; checking likely loses but avoids losing extra chips.  \n\n**Reason**:  \nMy hand has zero showdown value, but given pot size and opponent’s likely weak holding (they checked river), a bluff is risky with low fold equity. Since I’m ahead in the match, preserving chips is sensible. Checking ends the hand with minimal loss.  \n\n**Answer**: 0  \n\n---\n\nEvaluation: Hand extremely weak, bluff low success, pot small, check to minimize loss.  \nReason: Opponent likely has at least Ace-high or weak pair; bluff risky with little fold equity; checking avoids further chip loss.  \nAnswer: 0"}
